** An explicit cylinder from the cylinderGenerator (an O-grid of hexahedra, extruded along z): fixed at the
** bottom, compressed at the top and confined by a pressure on its mantle. The generator only describes the
** mesh, so the model runs distributed; its element sets and surfaces hold the part each process computes.
** Bit-identical to a serial run (U.ref).
*material, name=VonMises, id=myMaterial
210000, 0.3, 550, 1000, 200, 1400, 1

*modelGenerator, generator=cylinderGenerator, name=cyl
axis=z
radius=5.0
lY=10.0
nR=3
nY=4
elType=C3D8

*section, name=section1, material=myMaterial, type=solid
cyl_all

*job, name=cylinderjob, domain=3d
*solver, solver=NEDMPI, name=theSolver
output-frequency=1

*step, type=adaptiveForExplicitSimulations, solver=theSolver
maxInc=1e0, minInc=1e-2, maxNumInc=10000, maxIter=25, stepLength=1
>>dirichlet, name=bottom, nSet=cyl_bottom, field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=top, nSet=cyl_top, field=displacement, 3=-0.05
>>distributedload, name=confinement, surface=cyl_outer, magnitude=10, f(t)=t, type=pressure
